---
import CloudPage from '../../layouts/CloudPage.astro';
import { GCP_SERVICES } from '../../data/cloud-services';
import { SERVICE_COUNTS } from '../../data/services';

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
  "name": "floci-gcp",
  "applicationCategory": "DeveloperApplication",
  "operatingSystem": "Linux, macOS, Windows",
  "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD" },
  "license": "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT",
  "url": "https://floci.io/gcp/",
  "downloadUrl": "https://github.com/floci-io/floci-gcp",
  "description": "Free GCP emulator. Cloud Storage, Pub/Sub, Firestore, Secret Manager and more. No GCP account or billing required.",
  "keywords": "GCP emulator, Google Cloud local, Firestore emulator, Pub/Sub mock, Cloud Storage local"
};
---

<CloudPage
  cloud="gcp"
  title="floci-gcp: Local GCP Emulator"
  description="floci-gcp is a fast, free, open-source GCP emulator. Cloud Storage, Pub/Sub, Firestore, Datastore, Secret Manager, IAM, Managed Kafka, Cloud Tasks, Cloud Run, Cloud SQL, Cloud Functions, Cloud KMS, Cloud Logging, Cloud Monitoring, and Cloud Scheduler. No GCP account, no auth token, MIT licensed."
  canonical="https://floci.io/gcp/"
  ogImage="https://floci.io/og/gcp.png"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  docsHref="/floci-gcp/"
  services={GCP_SERVICES}
  servicesDesc="No project ID, no service account, no billing account. Every service fully unlocked."
>
  <section slot="quickstart" id="quickstart">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="section-label">Quick Start</div>
        <h2>Every way to run it.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">One CLI installs and runs all four emulators: use Homebrew, the install script or PowerShell. Or skip the CLI and run the Docker image.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- method tabs -->
      <div class="qs-method-tabs reveal reveal-delay-sm" id="qsMethodTabs">
        <button class="qs-method-tab active" data-qs="cli">floci CLI</button>
        <button class="qs-method-tab" data-qs="docker">Docker</button>
      </div>

      <!-- floci CLI panel -->
      <div id="qspanel-cli" class="qs-panel reveal reveal-delay">
        <div class="qs-grid">
          <div>
            <h3 class="qs-step">1 · Install floci CLI</h3>
            <div class="code-tabs" id="installTabs">
              <button class="code-tab active" data-tab="brew">Homebrew</button>
              <button class="code-tab" data-tab="curl">curl</button>
              <button class="code-tab" data-tab="ps">PowerShell</button>
            </div>
            <div id="itab-brew" class="code-block tabbed" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="cmd">brew install <span class="acc">floci-io/floci/floci</span></span></pre></div>
            <div id="itab-curl" class="code-block tabbed" style="display:none" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="cmd">curl -fsSL <span class="acc">https://floci.io/install.sh</span> | sh</span></pre></div>
            <div id="itab-ps" class="code-block tabbed" style="display:none" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="cmd">iwr <span class="acc">https://floci.io/install.ps1</span> | iex</span></pre></div>

            <h3 class="qs-step">2 · Start the emulator</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="cmd">floci gcp start</span></pre></div>

            <h3 class="qs-step">3 · Export env vars</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="cmd">eval $(floci gcp env)</span>
<span class="comment"># exports STORAGE_EMULATOR_HOST,</span>
<span class="comment"># PUBSUB_EMULATOR_HOST, FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST,</span>
<span class="comment"># DATASTORE_EMULATOR_HOST, SECRET_MANAGER_EMULATOR_HOST</span>

<span class="comment"># gcloud ignores those; point it at floci-gcp too</span>
<span class="comment"># (any token works locally)</span>
<span class="cmd">export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_API_ENDPOINT_OVERRIDES_STORAGE</span>=http://localhost:4588/
export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_CORE_PROJECT</span>=floci-local
export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_AUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN</span>=floci</span></pre></div>

            <h3 class="qs-step">4 · Upload a file</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="comment"># Create a bucket</span>
<span class="cmd">gcloud storage buckets create gs://<span class="str">my-bucket</span></span>

<span class="comment"># Write a file and upload it</span>
<span class="cmd">echo <span class="str">"No billing alert? Must be floci."</span> \
  &gt; hello-floci.txt
gcloud storage cp hello-floci.txt \
  gs://<span class="str">my-bucket</span>/hello-floci.txt</span>

<span class="comment"># Download it back and read it</span>
<span class="cmd">gcloud storage cp \
  gs://<span class="str">my-bucket</span>/hello-floci.txt \
  hello-back.txt
cat hello-back.txt</span></pre></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="qs-step">Teach your coding agent</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="comment"># Asks which agents to install it for</span>
<span class="cmd">npx skills add <span class="acc">floci-io/floci-cli</span></span></pre></div>
            <p class="qs-note">The Floci skill teaches Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Kiro and other coding agents to run the emulators with floci-cli.</p>

            <h3 class="qs-step">Other useful commands</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="comment"># Check status and server health</span>
<span class="cmd">floci gcp status</span>

<span class="comment"># List enabled services</span>
<span class="cmd">floci gcp services</span>

<span class="comment"># View logs</span>
<span class="cmd">floci gcp logs</span>

<span class="comment"># Stop the emulator</span>
<span class="cmd">floci gcp stop</span>

<span class="comment"># Export env for selected services only</span>
<span class="cmd">eval $(floci gcp env --service <span class="str">gcs,pubsub</span>)</span></pre></div>

            <h3 class="qs-step">Start with persistence</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="cmd">floci gcp start --persist <span class="acc">./data</span></span>
<span class="comment"># state survives container restarts</span></pre></div>

            <h3 class="qs-step">Diagnose issues</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="cmd">floci gcp doctor</span>
<span class="comment"># checks Docker, gcloud, connectivity</span></pre></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Docker panel -->
      <div id="qspanel-docker" class="qs-panel reveal reveal-delay" style="display:none">
        <div class="qs-grid">
          <div>
            <h3 class="qs-step">docker run</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="comment"># All services on :4588 · socket mount is for Cloud Run, Cloud SQL, GKE and Managed Kafka</span>
<span class="cmd">docker run -d --name floci-gcp \
  -p <span class="acc">4588:4588</span> \
  -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock \
  floci/floci-gcp:<span class="acc">latest</span></span></pre></div>

            <h3 class="qs-step">Set env vars</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="comment"># any token works locally</span>
<span class="cmd">export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_API_ENDPOINT_OVERRIDES_STORAGE</span>=http://localhost:4588/
export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_CORE_PROJECT</span>=floci-local
export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_AUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN</span>=floci</span></pre></div>

            <h3 class="qs-step">Upload a file</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="comment"># Create a bucket</span>
<span class="cmd">gcloud storage buckets create gs://<span class="str">my-bucket</span></span>

<span class="comment"># Write a file and upload it</span>
<span class="cmd">echo <span class="str">"No billing alert? Must be floci."</span> \
  &gt; hello-floci.txt
gcloud storage cp hello-floci.txt \
  gs://<span class="str">my-bucket</span>/hello-floci.txt</span>

<span class="comment"># Download it back and read it</span>
<span class="cmd">gcloud storage cp \
  gs://<span class="str">my-bucket</span>/hello-floci.txt \
  hello-back.txt
cat hello-back.txt</span></pre></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="qs-step">docker-compose</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="yaml"><pre
><span class="cmd">services:
  floci-gcp:
    image: floci/floci-gcp:<span class="acc">latest</span>
    ports:
      - <span class="str">"4588:4588"</span>
    volumes:
      - /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock</span></pre></div>

            <h3 class="qs-step">Python SDK</h3>
            <div class="code-block" data-lang="python"><pre
><span class="comment"># pip install google-cloud-storage</span>
<span class="cmd">import os
from google.cloud import storage

os.environ[<span class="str">"STORAGE_EMULATOR_HOST"</span>] = \
  <span class="str">"http://localhost:4588"</span>

client = storage.Client(project=<span class="str">"floci-local"</span>)
bucket = client.lookup_bucket(<span class="str">"my-bucket"</span>) or client.create_bucket(<span class="str">"my-bucket"</span>)
blob = bucket.blob(<span class="str">"hello-floci.txt"</span>)
blob.upload_from_string(
  <span class="str">"No billing alert? Must be floci."</span>
)</span></pre></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section slot="examples" id="examples">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="section-label">Examples</div>
        <h2>Client libraries and gcloud, side by side.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">Point your existing GCP client libraries at localhost:4588. No code changes beyond the endpoint.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ex-tabs reveal reveal-delay-sm" id="exTabs">
        <button class="ex-tab active" data-ex="storage">Cloud Storage</button>
        <button class="ex-tab" data-ex="pubsub">Pub/Sub</button>
        <button class="ex-tab" data-ex="firestore">Firestore</button>
        <button class="ex-tab" data-ex="secrets">Secret Manager</button>
      </div>

      <!-- Cloud Storage -->
      <div id="expanel-storage" class="ex-panel active reveal reveal-delay">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-label">Python · google-cloud-storage</div>
          <div class="code-block" data-lang="python"><pre
><span class="comment"># pip install google-cloud-storage</span>
<span class="cmd">import os
from google.cloud import storage

os.environ[<span class="str">"STORAGE_EMULATOR_HOST"</span>] = <span class="str">"http://localhost:4588"</span>
client = storage.Client(project=<span class="str">"floci-local"</span>)

<span class="comment"># create a bucket and upload a file</span>
bucket = client.lookup_bucket(<span class="str">"demo-bucket"</span>) or client.create_bucket(<span class="str">"demo-bucket"</span>)
blob = bucket.blob(<span class="str">"data/hello.txt"</span>)
blob.upload_from_string(<span class="str">"hello from floci-gcp!"</span>)

<span class="comment"># list objects in the bucket</span>
for b in client.list_blobs(<span class="str">"demo-bucket"</span>):
    print(b.name, b.size)

<span class="comment"># download and read back</span>
print(blob.download_as_text())</span></pre></div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="ex-label">gcloud CLI</div>
          <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="comment"># point gcloud at floci-gcp (any token works locally)</span>
<span class="cmd">export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_API_ENDPOINT_OVERRIDES_STORAGE</span>=http://localhost:4588/
export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_CORE_PROJECT</span>=floci-local
export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_AUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN</span>=floci

<span class="comment"># create a bucket</span>
gcloud storage buckets describe gs://<span class="str">demo-bucket</span> &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1 \
  || gcloud storage buckets create gs://<span class="str">demo-bucket</span>

<span class="comment"># upload a file</span>
echo <span class="str">"hello from floci-gcp!"</span> &gt; hello.txt
gcloud storage cp hello.txt gs://<span class="str">demo-bucket</span>/hello.txt

<span class="comment"># list objects</span>
gcloud storage ls gs://<span class="str">demo-bucket</span>

<span class="comment"># download it back</span>
gcloud storage cp gs://<span class="str">demo-bucket</span>/hello.txt -</span></pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Pub/Sub -->
      <div id="expanel-pubsub" class="ex-panel reveal reveal-delay">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-label">Python · google-cloud-pubsub</div>
          <div class="code-block" data-lang="python"><pre
><span class="comment"># pip install google-cloud-pubsub</span>
<span class="cmd">import os
from google.api_core.exceptions import AlreadyExists
from google.cloud import pubsub_v1

os.environ[<span class="str">"PUBSUB_EMULATOR_HOST"</span>] = <span class="str">"localhost:4588"</span>
project = <span class="str">"floci-local"</span>

publisher = pubsub_v1.PublisherClient()
subscriber = pubsub_v1.SubscriberClient()

<span class="comment"># create topic and subscription</span>
topic = publisher.topic_path(project, <span class="str">"my-topic"</span>)
sub = subscriber.subscription_path(project, <span class="str">"my-sub"</span>)
try:
    publisher.create_topic(request=&#123;<span class="str">"name"</span>: topic&#125;)
    subscriber.create_subscription(
        request=&#123;<span class="str">"name"</span>: sub, <span class="str">"topic"</span>: topic&#125;
    )
except AlreadyExists:
    pass  <span class="comment"># already created on an earlier run</span>

<span class="comment"># publish a message</span>
future = publisher.publish(topic, b<span class="str">"hello from floci-gcp!"</span>)
print(<span class="str">"Published: "</span> + str(future.result()))

<span class="comment"># pull and acknowledge</span>
resp = subscriber.pull(
    request=&#123;<span class="str">"subscription"</span>: sub, <span class="str">"max_messages"</span>: 1&#125;
)
for msg in resp.received_messages:
    print(msg.message.data.decode())
    subscriber.acknowledge(
        request=&#123;<span class="str">"subscription"</span>: sub,
                 <span class="str">"ack_ids"</span>: [msg.ack_id]&#125;
    )</span></pre></div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="ex-label">Node.js · @google-cloud/pubsub</div>
          <div class="code-block" data-lang="javascript"><pre
><span class="comment">// npm install @google-cloud/pubsub</span>
<span class="cmd">process.env.PUBSUB_EMULATOR_HOST = <span class="str">'localhost:4588'</span>;
const &#123; PubSub &#125; = require(<span class="str">'@google-cloud/pubsub'</span>);
const pubsub = new PubSub(&#123; projectId: <span class="str">'floci-local'</span> &#125;);

async function run() &#123;
  const [topic] = await pubsub
    .topic(<span class="str">'my-topic'</span>).get(&#123; autoCreate: true &#125;);
  const [sub] = await topic
    .subscription(<span class="str">'my-sub'</span>).get(&#123; autoCreate: true &#125;);

  <span class="comment">// publish a message</span>
  const msgId = await topic.publishMessage(&#123;
    data: Buffer.from(<span class="str">'hello from floci-gcp!'</span>),
  &#125;);
  console.log(<span class="str">'Published: '</span> + msgId);

  <span class="comment">// receive one message</span>
  sub.on(<span class="str">'message'</span>, msg =&gt; &#123;
    console.log(msg.data.toString());
    msg.ack();
    sub.removeAllListeners();
  &#125;);
&#125;
run();</span></pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Firestore -->
      <div id="expanel-firestore" class="ex-panel reveal reveal-delay">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-label">Python · google-cloud-firestore</div>
          <div class="code-block" data-lang="python"><pre
><span class="comment"># pip install google-cloud-firestore</span>
<span class="cmd">import os
from google.cloud import firestore

os.environ[<span class="str">"FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST"</span>] = <span class="str">"localhost:4588"</span>
db = firestore.Client(project=<span class="str">"floci-local"</span>)

<span class="comment"># write a document</span>
ref = db.collection(<span class="str">"users"</span>).document(<span class="str">"alice"</span>)
ref.set(&#123;<span class="str">"name"</span>: <span class="str">"Alice"</span>, <span class="str">"score"</span>: 42&#125;)

<span class="comment"># read it back</span>
doc = ref.get()
print(doc.to_dict())

<span class="comment"># query with a filter</span>
for doc in (
    db.collection(<span class="str">"users"</span>)
      .where(<span class="str">"score"</span>, <span class="str">"&gt;="</span>, 40)
      .stream()
):
    print(doc.id, doc.to_dict())</span></pre></div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="ex-label">Node.js · @google-cloud/firestore</div>
          <div class="code-block" data-lang="javascript"><pre
><span class="comment">// npm install @google-cloud/firestore</span>
<span class="cmd">process.env.FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST = <span class="str">'localhost:4588'</span>;
const &#123; Firestore &#125; = require(<span class="str">'@google-cloud/firestore'</span>);
const db = new Firestore(&#123; projectId: <span class="str">'floci-local'</span> &#125;);

async function run() &#123;
  <span class="comment">// write a document</span>
  const ref = db.collection(<span class="str">'users'</span>).doc(<span class="str">'alice'</span>);
  await ref.set(&#123;
    name: <span class="str">'Alice'</span>, score: 42, active: true
  &#125;);

  <span class="comment">// read it back</span>
  const doc = await ref.get();
  console.log(doc.data());

  <span class="comment">// query with a filter</span>
  const snap = await db.collection(<span class="str">'users'</span>)
    .where(<span class="str">'score'</span>, <span class="str">'&gt;='</span>, 40).get();
  snap.forEach(d =&gt; console.log(d.id, d.data()));
&#125;
run();</span></pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Secret Manager -->
      <div id="expanel-secrets" class="ex-panel reveal reveal-delay">
        <div>
          <div class="ex-label">Python · google-cloud-secret-manager</div>
          <div class="code-block" data-lang="python"><pre
><span class="comment"># pip install google-cloud-secret-manager</span>
<span class="cmd">import grpc
from google.api_core.exceptions import AlreadyExists
from google.cloud import secretmanager
from google.cloud.secretmanager_v1.services.secret_manager_service.transports.grpc import (
    SecretManagerServiceGrpcTransport,
)

<span class="comment"># the Python client ignores *_EMULATOR_HOST, so point it at floci-gcp over plain gRPC</span>
transport = SecretManagerServiceGrpcTransport(
    channel=grpc.insecure_channel(<span class="str">"localhost:4588"</span>)
)
client = secretmanager.SecretManagerServiceClient(transport=transport)
parent = <span class="str">"projects/floci-local"</span>

<span class="comment"># create the secret (skipped if it exists)</span>
name = parent + <span class="str">"/secrets/db-password"</span>
try:
    client.create_secret(request=&#123;
        <span class="str">"parent"</span>: parent,
        <span class="str">"secret_id"</span>: <span class="str">"db-password"</span>,
        <span class="str">"secret"</span>: &#123;<span class="str">"replication"</span>: &#123;<span class="str">"automatic"</span>: &#123;&#125;&#125;&#125;,
    &#125;)
except AlreadyExists:
    pass

<span class="comment"># store the value</span>
client.add_secret_version(request=&#123;
    <span class="str">"parent"</span>: name,
    <span class="str">"payload"</span>: &#123;<span class="str">"data"</span>: b<span class="str">"super-secret-value"</span>&#125;,
&#125;)

<span class="comment"># read the latest version</span>
version = name + <span class="str">"/versions/latest"</span>
resp = client.access_secret_version(request=&#123;<span class="str">"name"</span>: version&#125;)
print(resp.payload.data.decode())</span></pre></div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="ex-label">gcloud CLI</div>
          <div class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><pre
><span class="comment"># point gcloud at floci-gcp (any token works locally)</span>
<span class="cmd">export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_API_ENDPOINT_OVERRIDES_SECRETMANAGER</span>=http://localhost:4588/
export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_CORE_PROJECT</span>=floci-local
export <span class="acc">CLOUDSDK_AUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN</span>=floci

<span class="comment"># gcloud can't add secret versions on floci-gcp yet: store them from a</span>
<span class="comment"># client library (left), then read and list them here</span>
gcloud secrets list

<span class="comment"># read the latest version</span>
gcloud secrets versions access latest \
  --secret db-password</span></pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section slot="why" id="why">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="section-label">Why floci-gcp</div>
        <h2>The client libraries you already use.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">Point the official Google Cloud client libraries and gcloud at localhost:4588. No project, no service account key.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hairline reveal reveal-delay"><div class="hairline-grid cols-4">
        <div><h3>Emulator variables, set for you</h3><p><code>floci gcp env</code> exports STORAGE, PUBSUB, FIRESTORE, DATASTORE and SECRET_MANAGER <code>*_EMULATOR_HOST</code> variables for the libraries that read them.</p></div>
        <div><h3>gcloud included</h3><p>gcloud ignores those variables, so one endpoint override and any access token point it at floci-gcp instead.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Real containers where it matters</h3><p>Cloud Run, Cloud SQL, GKE (on k3s) and Managed Kafka (on Redpanda) run real containers through Docker.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Native binary speed</h3><p>Starts in 24 ms, idles at ~13 MiB and works offline, so CI never waits on the network.</p></div>
      </div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</CloudPage>

